Bluetooth: btmtk: fail the WMT command when its event never arrives

When a WMT command is woken without an event buffer, btmtk_usb_hci_wmt_sync()
returned success with the status the caller initialised, and left
BTMTK_TX_WAIT_VND_EVT set on the error path, so the next transaction saw a
stale wait. Return -EIO instead, and clear the wait flag on every exit.

The btusb.c half of this change, which released the runtime PM reference after
both MediaTek reset paths, is gone: Linux 7.3 fixes the same leak upstream by
dropping the reference through the BTUSB_RESET flag at disconnect, and keeping
a second put here would release it twice.

Source: Linux 7.3 drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c
SPDX-License-Identifier: ISC

--- a/btmtk.c
+++ b/btmtk.c
@@ -716,8 +716,10 @@
 		goto err_free_wc;
 	}

-	if (data->evt_skb == NULL)
+	if (data->evt_skb == NULL) {
+		err = -EIO;
 		goto err_free_wc;
+	}

 	wmt_evt = skb_pull_data(data->evt_skb, sizeof(*wmt_evt));
 	if (!wmt_evt) {
@@ -772,6 +774,7 @@
 	kfree_skb(data->evt_skb);
 	data->evt_skb = NULL;
 err_free_wc:
+	clear_bit(BTMTK_TX_WAIT_VND_EVT, &data->flags);
 	kfree(wc);
 	return err;
 }
